@host = http://localhost:5165

# The demo clinic, from:
#   dotnet run --project DYS.Molargo.API -- seed --demo
#
# The same clinic and the same credentials the desktop app seeds. Other users on it:
# cbrennan (reception), jellery (dentist), hito (hygienist) — all with the same password.

### Sign in. Everything below needs the token this returns.
# @name signIn
POST {{host}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clinicCode": "molargo-dental",
  "username": "rvance",
  "password": "molargo-demo"
}

### What the token says about the caller — tenant, provider, role, permissions.
@token = {{signIn.response.body.token}}

GET {{host}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Patients at this clinic. The tenant filter is on the context, not on this query.
GET {{host}}/patients?page=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Searched.
GET {{host}}/patients?search=yuen
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One patient.
GET {{host}}/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create one.
POST {{host}}/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "Patient",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-04-12",
  "mobile": "0400 000 000",
  "email": "test@example.test"
}

### Appointments. No range means the coming month — see the endpoint's note.
GET {{host}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A specific window.
GET {{host}}/appointments?from=2026-09-01&to=2026-12-31
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A course of treatment and its visits, in treatment order.
GET {{host}}/appointments/series/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Without a token — should be 401, not an empty list.
GET {{host}}/patients

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The app's own surface, by hand.
#
# The RPC routes are deliberately absent from the OpenAPI document — see
# RpcEndpoint — so Scalar will not show them and there is nothing to click.
# These are here so a service method can be called without the app, which is
# how you tell "the screen is wrong" from "the service is wrong".
#
# The route is POST /rpc/{Service}/{Method}/{arity}:
#   Service  the interface name without its I  — IPatientService -> PatientService
#   Method   exactly as declared               — SearchAsync
#   arity    arguments EXCLUDING the CancellationToken
#
# So Task<PagedResult<..>> SearchAsync(PatientQuery query, CancellationToken ct)
# is arity 1, not 2. Get it wrong and the answer says so:
#   {"error":"PatientService has no SearchAsync taking 2 argument(s)."}
#
# The body is always a JSON ARRAY of the arguments, in declaration order.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### One page of patients. Arity 1 — the query object is the only argument.
POST {{host}}/rpc/PatientService/SearchAsync/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

[{ "SearchTerm": null, "Page": 0, "PageSize": 17 }]

### A method with no arguments at all. The body is still an array — an empty one.
POST {{host}}/rpc/AdminService/GetSitesAsync/0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

[]

### Two arguments, positional. Nulls are sent, not omitted.
POST {{host}}/rpc/PatientService/FindEmailHolderAsync/2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

["someone@example.test", null]

### A guard, which re-reads the staff record rather than trusting the token.
POST {{host}}/rpc/PracticeGuard/IsOwnerAsync/0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

[]

### A name that does not exist — 404 naming what was not found.
POST {{host}}/rpc/NoSuchService/GetAsync/0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

[]
